meta {
  name: Anonymous Signup
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{protocol}}://{{baseUrl}}/mobile-test-track-signup
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Origin: http://localhost:3000
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "test@example.com",
    "ios": true,
    "android": false,
    "turnstileToken": "0.test-token",
    "website": ""
  }
}

docs {
  Opts an anonymous visitor into the internal mobile test track by email,
  without requiring an account. Creates (or finds) a passwordless Auth0
  "email" connection user and writes the same opt-in fields used by the
  authenticated `/profile/mobile-test-track-signup` endpoint.

  Idempotent per email/platform — resubmitting a platform already opted
  into is a no-op. Notifies via the same GitHub issue mechanism as the
  authenticated flow (label `mobile-test-user-opt-in`) — the issue includes
  only the Auth0 user ID, **never the email or any hint of it**.

  Public/unauthenticated, so it's gated the same way `/issues` is:
  - Turnstile CAPTCHA verification (required, not best-effort)
  - Per-IP rate limiting (5 requests/hour, separate quota from `/issues`)
  - Honeypot field (`website`) — if non-empty, silently returns a fake
    success without creating anything

  ## Authentication
  None — this endpoint requires no login.

  ## Prerequisites
  - Auth0 tenant must have the "email" passwordless connection enabled
    (with it turned OFF for any real user-facing application, so it never
    appears as a login option for real users)
  - The Auth0 M2M application needs `create:users` scope in addition to
    `read:users`/`update:users`
  - GitHub credentials must be configured (required here, not optional,
    since Turnstile verification is the only anti-abuse gate)

  ## Request Body
  - `email` (string, required): Must contain "@"
  - `ios` (boolean, optional, default false): Opt into the iOS test track
  - `android` (boolean, optional, default false): Opt into the Android test track
  - At least one of `ios`/`android` must be true
  - `turnstileToken` (string, required): Cloudflare Turnstile CAPTCHA token
  - `website` (string, optional): Honeypot field — should always be empty

  ## Responses
  - `200`: Opt-in state reflects the email's current overall opt-in status
    ```json
    {
      "optInMobileTestTrackIos": true,
      "optInMobileTestTrackAndroid": false
    }
    ```
  - `400`: Invalid email, or neither `ios` nor `android` was true
  - `403`: Turnstile verification failed
  - `429`: Rate limit exceeded (5 signups per IP per hour)
}
